diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:5:5: Emerald has no `static`
      static var made = 0
      ^^^^^^
A member that belongs to the type puts the type's name in front instead, as in `var Counter.made = ...`.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:6:5: `count` needs `var` or `const` in front
      count: Int
      ^^^^^
A stored field says whether it can change, as in `var count: ...`.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:8:5: a constructor is written `constructor`
      init(count: Int) {
      ^^^^
Write `constructor(...) { ... }`. Inside it, `self` is the value being built.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:12:5: Emerald has no `static`
      static func make(): Counter {
      ^^^^^^
A member that belongs to the type puts the type's name in front instead, as in `func Counter.make()`.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:16:10: a constructor is written without `func`
      func constructor(count: Int) {
           ^^^^^^^^^^^
Write `constructor(...) { ... }` directly inside the struct.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:19:15: `self` is not listed as a parameter
      func grow(self, by: Int) {
                ^^^^
Every method and constructor already has `self`. Remove it from the parameter list.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:22:19: `doubled` needs a type before its body
      const doubled {
                    ^
A property states the type it gives, as in `const doubled: Float { ... }`.
diagnostics/struct-member-habits.em:32:12: a named argument is written with `:`
  greet(name = "Ava")
             ^
Write `name: ...` instead of `name = ...`.
